278
00:17:17,892 --> 00:17:18,975
I mean,

279
00:17:18,976 --> 00:17:21,228
are we trying to see
which one of us did worse?

280
00:17:21,937 --> 00:17:22,938
Hey, Seon.

281
00:17:23,397 --> 00:17:24,981
Let's not do this.

282
00:17:24,982 --> 00:17:27,193
Do you really want a divorce?

283
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:31,321
Yes, even if we each give in
a hundred times and divorce,

284
00:17:31,322 --> 00:17:33,156
we can't do this now.

285
00:17:33,157 --> 00:17:34,949
How many times do I have to say it?

286
00:17:34,950 --> 00:17:38,244
If we just wait a little,
we'll earn enough to live for a lifetime.

287
00:17:38,245 --> 00:17:40,790
No, it's going to blow up bigger.

288
00:17:41,123 --> 00:17:41,957
Seon.

289
00:17:43,209 --> 00:17:44,877
Seriously, now.

290
00:17:45,461 --> 00:17:48,129
Once this is all over,
it'll just be a memory.

291
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:49,757
It'll be nothing.

292
00:17:51,258 --> 00:17:52,551
Do you

293
00:17:53,010 --> 00:17:54,719
really not understand why

294
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,223
I'm talking about divorce
and trying to sell the building now?

295
00:17:57,473 --> 00:17:59,058
It's what you just mentioned.

296
00:17:59,725 --> 00:18:02,394
That business you're trying to do
with Real Capital.

297
00:18:02,395 --> 00:18:04,188
I'm trying to ruin that.

298
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:07,607
Seriously, Gi Su-jong,

299
00:18:07,608 --> 00:18:09,276
you've lost all sense
of feelings now, have you?

300
00:18:09,694 --> 00:18:11,945
Hey, I'm really worried
about you.

301
00:18:11,946 --> 00:18:14,115
You'll be in big trouble
if you keep this up.

302
00:18:14,573 --> 00:18:16,117
What is this?

303
00:18:16,784 --> 00:18:18,159
Are you threatening me?

304
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:20,287
No, that's not it.

305
00:18:20,955 --> 00:18:23,498
You know about Real Capital, don't you?

306
00:18:23,499 --> 00:18:25,625
You need to follow the situation.

307
00:18:25,626 --> 00:18:28,129
After all that you suffered,
how can you say things like this?

308
00:18:29,004 --> 00:18:31,382
I can't do this. Once this is over,

309
00:18:31,799 --> 00:18:32,924
let's talk about divorce again.

310
00:18:32,925 --> 00:18:33,801
Just listen to me.

311
00:18:36,095 --> 00:18:38,179
If you don't want to sign
the agreement, then don't.

312
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:39,306
I'll just file a lawsuit.

313
00:18:44,603 --> 00:18:45,604
Damn it.

314
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:53,362
You're quick.
We've secured all the revised land lots.

315
00:18:55,489 --> 00:18:58,200
Now, let's get to the important stuff.

316
00:18:59,326 --> 00:19:01,454
But is there anything
more important than this?

317
00:19:01,954 --> 00:19:03,038
Jeon Yi-gyeong.

318
00:19:03,456 --> 00:19:05,707
She could suddenly appear,
demanding ownership,

319
00:19:05,708 --> 00:19:07,959
and breaking the contract,
which would just be a hassle.

320
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:09,003
I'll take care of it.

321
00:19:11,255 --> 00:19:13,006
But they have a weakness too.

322
00:19:13,007 --> 00:19:14,174
That won't happen.

323
00:19:14,175 --> 00:19:16,760
If Jeon Yi-gyeong dies now,

324
00:19:16,761 --> 00:19:18,971
the Pyeong-buk Gwan contract is gone.

325
00:19:19,263 --> 00:19:22,683
And if there's no heir
for Pyeong-buk Gwan,

326
00:19:23,058 --> 00:19:25,853
then the court will take control.

327
00:19:26,187 --> 00:19:27,187
Do you want to see that?

328
00:19:27,188 --> 00:19:28,521
That will be inconvenient.

329
00:19:28,522 --> 00:19:30,775
It's much easier to manage it
like we are now.

330
00:19:33,986 --> 00:19:37,490
Wow, you've really grown up, Mr. Gi.

331
00:19:40,326 --> 00:19:41,410
Hold on a second.

332
00:19:43,746 --> 00:19:45,164
Gi Su-jong speaking.

333
00:19:46,207 --> 00:19:48,792
Oh, that property is not for sale.

334
00:19:48,793 --> 00:19:51,086
We're not selling it. Bye.

335
00:19:52,755 --> 00:19:53,922
Seyoon Building

336
00:19:53,923 --> 00:19:56,425
had a banner hanging like this.

337
00:19:57,051 --> 00:19:58,052
Wife issues?

338
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:00,595
Just some minor problems.

339
00:20:00,596 --> 00:20:02,305
Emotional stuff, you know.

340
00:20:02,306 --> 00:20:03,432
Don't worry about it.

341
00:20:05,392 --> 00:20:09,020
How can I not worry?

342
00:20:09,021 --> 00:20:12,024
If you get divorced,
part of your share will go to your wife.

343
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:15,611
Jeon Yi-gyeong wasn't the problem.
It was Kim Seon.

344
00:20:17,196 --> 00:20:18,155
So?

345
00:20:18,823 --> 00:20:21,617
Wow, we can't let
Kim Seon live, right?

346
00:20:22,827 --> 00:20:23,953
There's a lot to do.

347
00:20:25,955 --> 00:20:27,957
What are you all talking about?

348
00:20:31,335 --> 00:20:32,753
What do you think?

349
00:20:38,634 --> 00:20:39,844
SEON

350
00:20:48,143 --> 00:20:49,270
Why isn't she answering...

351
00:20:55,776 --> 00:20:56,569
What’s going on?

352
00:20:59,446 --> 00:21:00,322
What's wrong with this?

353
00:21:10,082 --> 00:21:10,875
Seon!

354
00:21:15,421 --> 00:21:16,297
Hey, Kim Seon.

355
00:21:26,599 --> 00:21:27,850
Da-rae!

356
00:21:29,393 --> 00:21:31,854
Dad needs to talk to you.

357
00:21:34,356 --> 00:21:38,027
Mom told
me not to talk to you.

358
00:21:38,611 --> 00:21:41,029
Please listen to me, okay?

359
00:21:41,030 --> 00:21:44,240
Dad wants to protect

360
00:21:44,241 --> 00:21:46,159
you and Mom, okay?

361
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:47,411
Where's Mom?

362
00:21:48,913 --> 00:21:53,250
I don't know.
I still have class. I have to go in.

363
00:22:00,674 --> 00:22:02,175
Real Capital is

364
00:22:02,176 --> 00:22:03,385
targeting Seon.

365
00:22:04,219 --> 00:22:05,429
Is this reliable information?

366
00:22:06,221 --> 00:22:08,807
We don't have Gyun's USB drive anymore.
What's the reason?

367
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:11,059
Well, from their perspective,

368
00:22:11,060 --> 00:22:13,394
they just need to stamp the last document.

369
00:22:13,395 --> 00:22:14,396
Seon is

370
00:22:14,813 --> 00:22:16,482
considered the last obstacle.

371
00:22:17,107 --> 00:22:17,942
So what?

372
00:22:18,442 --> 00:22:20,110
You know they're working on this.

373
00:22:20,444 --> 00:22:22,112
They will definitely kill Seon.

374
00:22:22,821 --> 00:22:24,615
I see what you're saying,

375
00:22:25,783 --> 00:22:28,868
but what can the police do about
an event that hasn't happened yet?

376
00:22:28,869 --> 00:22:29,954
We need to set a trap.

377
00:22:31,330 --> 00:22:32,623
To prevent them from crossing that line.

378
00:22:35,709 --> 00:22:38,045
With Oh Dong-ki,
it was you who set a trap, right?

379
00:22:40,297 --> 00:22:41,256
No.

380
00:22:41,924 --> 00:22:42,841
With that...

381
00:22:44,176 --> 00:22:47,096
After we deal with them,
I'll explain everything honestly.

382
00:22:47,513 --> 00:22:49,181
We need your help right now.

383
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:51,976
We have to get revenge for Gyun.

384
00:23:06,782 --> 00:23:08,617
Ju-ran, is this really okay?

385
00:23:09,326 --> 00:23:10,536
It's an unauthorized operation.

386
00:23:11,495 --> 00:23:13,122
Without the sergeant,
who do we even ask for permission?

387
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:15,666
Well, that's true, but...

388
00:23:16,333 --> 00:23:18,419
If we catch them, it all gets solved.

389
00:23:20,796 --> 00:23:22,047
This time, we'll definitely catch them.

390
00:23:22,715 --> 00:23:23,799
Okay...

391
00:23:40,607 --> 00:23:41,567
Hey, Seon.

392
00:23:43,861 --> 00:23:45,362
Why haven't you been reachable?

393
00:23:56,331 --> 00:23:57,833
Damn it.

394
00:24:07,384 --> 00:24:08,010
Yes?

395
00:24:13,307 --> 00:24:15,768
Your wife and Da-rae have been taken
to the place you mentioned.

396
00:24:25,486 --> 00:24:26,320
Hello.

397
00:24:27,821 --> 00:24:28,781
Take care of Da-rae.

398
00:24:35,496 --> 00:24:36,080
Let's go.

399
00:24:37,122 --> 00:24:37,831
Yes.

400
00:24:43,170 --> 00:24:43,921
Yes.

401
00:24:44,254 --> 00:24:45,379
This is a listening device.

402
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:46,757
Just put it in your pocket.

403
00:24:48,217 --> 00:24:49,592
Don't lead the testimony.

404
00:24:49,593 --> 00:24:51,261
Be careful with specific questions.

405
00:24:55,015 --> 00:24:56,891
CERTIFICATE OF ALL REGISTERED MATTERS

406
00:24:56,892 --> 00:24:58,268
33 Pyeong-buk Gwan, Sejeong-ro 3-gil,
Yongdaemun-gu, Seoul

407
00:25:02,314 --> 00:25:04,607
OWNER: NOUVEAU CITY DEVELOPMENT

408
00:25:04,608 --> 00:25:06,610
It got delayed a bit,

409
00:25:07,152 --> 00:25:09,029
but there's no problem with the item.

410
00:25:09,404 --> 00:25:11,656
But the headquarters is curious.

411
00:25:11,657 --> 00:25:14,201
Why didn't you report Nam Sang-ho's death?

412
00:25:15,369 --> 00:25:18,956
He cheated and then committed suicide.
Do I need to report that too?

413
00:25:19,623 --> 00:25:24,335
But Nam Sang-ho
still has a role.

414
00:25:24,336 --> 00:25:25,963
It's gotten a bit complicated.

415
00:25:29,174 --> 00:25:31,468
Just report it when I tell you to.

416
00:25:37,391 --> 00:25:38,183
By the way,

417
00:25:39,434 --> 00:25:41,478
Seyoon Building was listed for quick sale.

418
00:25:42,104 --> 00:25:43,605
There's no issue with it, right?

419
00:25:45,399 --> 00:25:48,318
The headquarters has
already been patient enough.

420
00:25:49,278 --> 00:25:50,904
Let's wrap this up quickly.

421
00:25:58,120 --> 00:25:59,413
What brings you here at this hour?

422
00:25:59,580 --> 00:26:01,206
Well, I texted you earlier.

423
00:26:01,415 --> 00:26:02,666
- You texted?
- Yes.

424
00:26:06,628 --> 00:26:08,338
Oh, you did. Sorry.

425
00:26:09,214 --> 00:26:10,299
Is it something urgent?

426
00:26:10,799 --> 00:26:13,050
Well, I have
something to discuss.

427
00:26:13,051 --> 00:26:15,303
But that person earlier, was he a lawyer?

428
00:26:15,304 --> 00:26:16,013
Yes.

429
00:26:18,432 --> 00:26:19,433
I got this.

430
00:26:21,185 --> 00:26:23,020
It looked delicious.

431
00:26:26,190 --> 00:26:27,566
But I don't eat sweets.

432
00:26:28,525 --> 00:26:29,526
I only eat low-calorie foods.

433
00:26:30,611 --> 00:26:32,862
But it's okay
to have a little sometimes.

434
00:26:32,863 --> 00:26:34,072
It helps relieve fatigue too.

435
00:26:34,448 --> 00:26:37,826
Why are you suddenly
trying to make me eat sweets?

436
00:26:38,702 --> 00:26:39,827
Tell me.

437
00:26:39,828 --> 00:26:40,871
What's the problem?

438
00:26:42,164 --> 00:26:43,957
Well, problems...

439
00:26:44,666 --> 00:26:45,959
There are a few.

440
00:26:46,835 --> 00:26:50,087
My life is falling apart.
It's a complete mess.

441
00:26:50,088 --> 00:26:51,757
Come on, how is it a mess?

442
00:26:52,591 --> 00:26:55,051
If you deal with a few minor issues,

443
00:26:55,052 --> 00:26:56,385
you'll be successful.

444
00:26:56,386 --> 00:26:57,720
Minor issues?

445
00:26:57,721 --> 00:26:59,723
It's not as easy as it sounds.

446
00:27:00,432 --> 00:27:04,394
My wife wants a divorce
and I might lose the building.

447
00:27:05,354 --> 00:27:08,607
I think this will hinder our business.

448
00:27:09,524 --> 00:27:10,359
Right?

449
00:27:11,193 --> 00:27:13,153
Why did you even start a family?

450
00:27:17,574 --> 00:27:20,619
So, this is a sensitive topic,

451
00:27:21,870 --> 00:27:24,623
but can you kill my wife?

452
00:27:26,959 --> 00:27:29,002
I mean,
you killed Jung Chang-su,

453
00:27:30,128 --> 00:27:33,048
my brother-in-law, and Mr. Nam too.

454
00:27:33,715 --> 00:27:35,676
You've taken care of them all.

455
00:27:37,761 --> 00:27:38,804
There's more.

456
00:27:39,513 --> 00:27:40,222
Who?

457
00:27:40,973 --> 00:27:42,140
Morgan Lee.

458
00:27:42,933 --> 00:27:44,268
He was my boss.

459
00:27:45,227 --> 00:27:46,228
I killed him.

460
00:27:47,145 --> 00:27:48,563
For risk management.

461
00:27:50,482 --> 00:27:51,817
It's business.

462
00:27:54,653 --> 00:27:55,487
Oh...

463
00:27:59,741 --> 00:28:00,742
Tomorrow night.

464
00:28:02,286 --> 00:28:03,912
My wife will be home alone.

465
00:28:04,329 --> 00:28:06,707
Our daughter is away on a trip
and I'll be out too.

466
00:28:07,499 --> 00:28:10,377
One person should be
easy to handle, right?

467
00:28:10,627 --> 00:28:11,752
That way,

468
00:28:11,753 --> 00:28:14,088
we can eliminate that risk

469
00:28:14,089 --> 00:28:16,717
and move on to our next step,
don't you think?

470
00:28:39,156 --> 00:28:40,406
I'm sorry.

471
00:28:40,407 --> 00:28:43,076
You were trying to be serious,
but I laughed.

472
00:28:43,994 --> 00:28:47,956
I really chose a good partner.

473
00:28:51,126 --> 00:28:51,835
So,

474
00:28:52,586 --> 00:28:53,378
how about it?

475
00:28:54,379 --> 00:28:55,422
Can you do it?

476
00:28:56,506 --> 00:28:57,798
I can do it today too.

477
00:28:57,799 --> 00:28:59,426
Oh, not today.

478
00:29:02,304 --> 00:29:05,057
She's staying home
with a nurse friend today.

479
00:29:05,724 --> 00:29:09,561
Even in the middle of a divorce case,
you keep up with the news well.

480
00:29:10,854 --> 00:29:14,358
We're not separated yet,
so I can know the details.

481
00:29:19,112 --> 00:29:20,489
You want to kill her?

482
00:29:24,493 --> 00:29:26,827
Wow, you're a bad person.

483
00:29:26,828 --> 00:29:28,121
A psychopath!

484
00:29:29,122 --> 00:29:31,624
I mean, are there
any good people out there?

485
00:29:31,625 --> 00:29:33,251
It's just survival instinct.

486
00:29:38,131 --> 00:29:39,758
Should I take a bite?

487
00:30:28,223 --> 00:30:29,432
Please wear this.

488
00:30:29,433 --> 00:30:30,058
Okay.

489
00:30:40,193 --> 00:30:40,902
Get ready.

490
00:31:12,100 --> 00:31:13,602
Is Da-rae doing okay?

491
00:31:18,106 --> 00:31:19,900
Da-rae is asleep.

492
00:32:30,011 --> 00:32:31,303
Something feels off.

493
00:32:31,304 --> 00:32:32,389
It's been too long.

494
00:33:16,933 --> 00:33:19,269
I'm running a bit late
with things at headquarters.

495
00:33:20,854 --> 00:33:22,314
You don't need to come right now.

496
00:33:40,373 --> 00:33:41,333
Yes, talk to me.

497
00:33:43,168 --> 00:33:45,211
Mr. Gi, we lost her.

498
00:33:45,545 --> 00:33:47,213
What do you mean you lost her?

499
00:33:53,178 --> 00:33:54,595
Hurry over.

500
00:33:54,596 --> 00:33:55,929
There's no time to buy a cake this time.

501
00:33:55,930 --> 00:33:57,098
Damn it.

502
00:34:01,978 --> 00:34:05,190
DAD

503
00:35:02,414 --> 00:35:03,540
Hello.

504
00:35:04,249 --> 00:35:05,125
Yi-gyeong?

505
00:35:07,585 --> 00:35:08,753
Jeon Yi-gyeong, right?

506
00:35:09,838 --> 00:35:11,589
Where are you going?

507
00:35:12,090 --> 00:35:14,049
I have so much

508
00:35:14,050 --> 00:35:16,010
to talk about with you.

509
00:35:23,059 --> 00:35:24,978
Oh, my heart is racing.

510
00:35:31,151 --> 00:35:32,193
Yi-gyeong!

511
00:35:43,371 --> 00:35:44,539
Yi-gyeong.

512
00:35:48,877 --> 00:35:50,295
Jeez.

513
00:35:51,463 --> 00:35:54,841
Which way did she go?

514
00:35:56,634 --> 00:35:57,635
Are you here?

515
00:36:03,057 --> 00:36:04,142
You're going to do it like this?

516
00:36:06,186 --> 00:36:07,187
Damn.

517
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:13,359
Damn it!

518
00:36:33,421 --> 00:36:34,339
Damn it...

519
00:36:36,424 --> 00:36:38,176
Who is it?

520
00:36:40,094 --> 00:36:41,554
This is fun.

521
00:36:49,395 --> 00:36:50,480
Oh...

522
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:53,525
I'm out of breath.

523
00:38:07,682 --> 00:38:08,433
Look here.

524
00:38:23,323 --> 00:38:24,782
What's wrong? What happened?

525
00:38:29,120 --> 00:38:33,833
Auntie! I won't leave you alone!

526
00:41:09,280 --> 00:41:10,865
Hey, you made it.

527
00:41:11,657 --> 00:41:13,493
This is perfect timing.

528
00:41:18,206 --> 00:41:19,664
I'm glad I wasn't late.

529
00:41:19,665 --> 00:41:23,086
Don't worry.
I won't kill your daughter.

530
00:41:23,628 --> 00:41:25,797
She can't say anything anyway.

531
00:41:27,090 --> 00:41:29,217
But you never know.

532
00:41:30,384 --> 00:41:33,096
I could change my mind and just...

533
00:41:35,181 --> 00:41:36,015
Let's stop this.

534
00:41:36,724 --> 00:41:38,726
I'll give up all my shares
in Nouveau City.

535
00:41:40,561 --> 00:41:41,479
Why?

536
00:41:42,605 --> 00:41:44,357
You came all the way here for that.

537
00:41:46,609 --> 00:41:48,360
No, you see,

538
00:41:48,361 --> 00:41:49,987
I'm not fit for that.

539
00:41:53,825 --> 00:41:55,118
That's a bit disappointing.

540
00:41:56,786 --> 00:41:57,829
Mr. Gi,

541
00:41:59,330 --> 00:42:02,250
I thought we were the same kind.

542
00:42:04,085 --> 00:42:06,003
You thought I would be fooled, right?

543
00:42:08,005 --> 00:42:10,549
I'll give up on Nouveau City.

544
00:42:10,550 --> 00:42:12,760
You can take it all, okay?

545
00:42:13,010 --> 00:42:15,304
You'll give up your stake
in Nouveau City?

546
00:42:17,765 --> 00:42:19,892
Oh, that's a bummer.

547
00:42:24,647 --> 00:42:25,356
Huh?

548
00:42:28,234 --> 00:42:29,109
Deal.

549
00:42:29,110 --> 00:42:30,570
Then you take care

550
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:32,947
of Jeon Yi-gyeong

551
00:42:33,531 --> 00:42:36,033
and I'll send your daughter off nicely.

552
00:42:42,331 --> 00:42:43,124
Wait a second.

553
00:42:44,834 --> 00:42:46,252
I have something I'm curious about first.

554
00:42:47,253 --> 00:42:49,087
How much more

555
00:42:49,088 --> 00:42:51,048
are you trying to earn by doing this?

556
00:42:51,591 --> 00:42:53,176
I'm really curious about that.

557
00:42:54,844 --> 00:42:56,470
I don't earn much.

558
00:42:57,555 --> 00:42:58,556
And

559
00:42:59,390 --> 00:43:01,184
there's something
more important than money.

560
00:43:02,059 --> 00:43:03,144
Something more fun.

561
00:43:05,271 --> 00:43:06,522
You're still alive.

562
00:43:07,148 --> 00:43:08,024
You're late.

563
00:43:08,399 --> 00:43:09,566
What's going on?

564
00:43:09,567 --> 00:43:11,194
Mr. Gi asked me

565
00:43:11,736 --> 00:43:13,237
how much money

566
00:43:13,696 --> 00:43:14,655
I make.

567
00:43:15,823 --> 00:43:17,325
Is that really important?

568
00:43:19,785 --> 00:43:21,119
I'm curious about that too.

569
00:43:21,120 --> 00:43:22,872
Anyway, I don't know.

570
00:43:24,123 --> 00:43:26,291
Let's wrap this up
and talk outside.

571
00:43:26,292 --> 00:43:27,168
I'm hungry.

572
00:43:27,960 --> 00:43:30,296
And we need to save his dear daughter.

573
00:43:36,260 --> 00:43:37,178
Ten.

574
00:43:38,429 --> 00:43:39,180
Nine.

575
00:43:40,139 --> 00:43:41,057
Eight.

576
00:43:42,058 --> 00:43:42,850
Seven.

577
00:43:44,227 --> 00:43:44,977
Six.

578
00:43:46,437 --> 00:43:48,438
Quit dragging it out

579
00:43:48,439 --> 00:43:50,107
before I change my mind.

580
00:44:01,661 --> 00:44:03,412
Undertaker, you want to just
pull the trigger?

581
00:44:04,455 --> 00:44:05,039
Sure.

582
00:45:29,498 --> 00:45:32,084
INTERROGATION ROOM

583
00:45:32,209 --> 00:45:34,587
So, you only heard
the gunfire, right?

584
00:45:35,087 --> 00:45:35,796
Yes.

585
00:45:37,089 --> 00:45:39,925
I was at the scene,

586
00:45:41,052 --> 00:45:44,055
and Jonah and Mr. Kim Chun-gil

587
00:45:44,930 --> 00:45:46,432
were already dead.

588
00:45:47,975 --> 00:45:49,894
But how did they know it was a trap?

589
00:45:51,228 --> 00:45:52,229
I don't know.

590
00:45:53,606 --> 00:45:55,316
Well, the information
could have leaked.

591
00:45:55,775 --> 00:45:57,068
I'm not sure.

592
00:46:01,489 --> 00:46:04,367
Why do you think
all these deaths happened?

593
00:46:07,453 --> 00:46:09,789
I don't know.

594
00:46:13,793 --> 00:46:14,960
Yes.

595
00:46:16,087 --> 00:46:17,963
It's all because of the Seyoon Building.

596
00:46:18,839 --> 00:46:19,632
What?

597
00:46:20,424 --> 00:46:22,051
Yi-gyeong's kidnapping,

598
00:46:23,094 --> 00:46:24,387
Oh Dong-ki's death,

599
00:46:24,887 --> 00:46:28,808
Jeon Yang-ja's death,
and my friend Hwal-sung's death,

600
00:46:29,725 --> 00:46:31,727
they all happened
at Seyoon Building, right?

601
00:46:32,353 --> 00:46:33,270
Well, I have

602
00:46:34,021 --> 00:46:35,606
no legal responsibility,

603
00:46:36,315 --> 00:46:37,817
but I do consider myself guilty.

604
00:46:42,488 --> 00:46:43,613
Are there

605
00:46:43,614 --> 00:46:45,824
any other questions?

606
00:46:45,825 --> 00:46:46,826
Hold on.

607
00:46:48,202 --> 00:46:50,954
When you said you'll tell the whole truth,

608
00:46:50,955 --> 00:46:51,872
is this what you meant?

609
00:46:53,416 --> 00:46:55,042
They were all just accidents.

610
00:46:56,877 --> 00:46:58,379
No one expected it.

611
00:46:59,213 --> 00:47:00,588
Even for you,

612
00:47:00,589 --> 00:47:01,966
wasn't shooting Oh Dong-ki

613
00:47:03,008 --> 00:47:04,051
an accident?

614
00:47:08,264 --> 00:47:11,182
If there's anything else I can help with,

615
00:47:11,183 --> 00:47:12,351
just feel free to contact me.

616
00:47:32,621 --> 00:47:33,998
What happened?

617
00:47:34,540 --> 00:47:35,415
What about Da-rae?

618
00:47:35,416 --> 00:47:36,292
She's safe.

619
00:47:36,750 --> 00:47:37,877
Right now, she's in the hospital.

620
00:47:39,753 --> 00:47:42,131
And Jonah is deceased.

621
00:47:43,591 --> 00:47:44,508
Deceased?

622
00:47:45,593 --> 00:47:46,635
You mean she's dead?

623
00:47:47,303 --> 00:47:48,179
How?

624
00:47:48,471 --> 00:47:49,680
She was shot dead.

625
00:47:51,849 --> 00:47:53,766
It looks like
a professional did it,

626
00:47:53,767 --> 00:47:55,478
but details are still under investigation.

627
00:47:57,897 --> 00:47:59,315
There shouldn't be any immediate danger.

628
00:48:00,357 --> 00:48:01,859
Still, be careful just in case.

629
00:48:02,526 --> 00:48:04,069
We'll keep monitoring as well.

630
00:48:07,281 --> 00:48:09,116
But why did they spare you?

631
00:48:11,494 --> 00:48:12,578
I don't know.

632
00:48:13,287 --> 00:48:14,246
I'm not sure.

633
00:48:19,585 --> 00:48:20,294
What is this?

634
00:48:20,669 --> 00:48:22,004
I came to talk business.

635
00:48:22,630 --> 00:48:23,631
But this is

636
00:48:24,340 --> 00:48:25,925
something that can't leak.

637
00:48:26,634 --> 00:48:27,426
Okay.

638
00:48:27,927 --> 00:48:29,470
Tonight, your employee

639
00:48:30,387 --> 00:48:33,389
is planning to kill my wife.

640
00:48:33,390 --> 00:48:35,768
But it's a trap.

641
00:48:36,393 --> 00:48:38,771
The police are lying in wait.

642
00:48:39,396 --> 00:48:41,398
Why are you telling me this?

643
00:48:41,690 --> 00:48:44,193
If your employee gets caught,
it'll be exhausting.

644
00:48:45,236 --> 00:48:48,113
So, I've been thinking.
How about we just...

645
00:48:48,739 --> 00:48:49,532
Just?

646
00:48:49,907 --> 00:48:51,659
How about we just kill her?

647
00:48:54,870 --> 00:48:57,205
I'll just pretend I didn't hear that.

648
00:48:57,206 --> 00:48:58,707
I'm not interested in that.

649
00:49:01,460 --> 00:49:02,503
If you see this,

650
00:49:03,170 --> 00:49:04,755
you might become interested.

651
00:49:07,883 --> 00:49:09,843
I mean,
you killed Jung Chang-su,

652
00:49:11,011 --> 00:49:12,221
my brother-in-law,

653
00:49:12,555 --> 00:49:14,014
and Mr. Nam too.

654
00:49:14,598 --> 00:49:16,684
You've taken care of them all.

655
00:49:17,560 --> 00:49:18,686
There's more.

656
00:49:19,520 --> 00:49:20,271
Who?

657
00:49:20,938 --> 00:49:22,189
Lee Morgan.

658
00:49:22,898 --> 00:49:24,358
He was my boss.

659
00:49:25,109 --> 00:49:26,193
I killed him.

660
00:49:31,031 --> 00:49:33,074
If you want to start a business in Korea,

661
00:49:33,075 --> 00:49:34,451
you need a partner.

662
00:49:35,786 --> 00:49:38,414
You know I'm in charge
of Nouveau City, right?

663
00:49:39,123 --> 00:49:39,999
So what?

664
00:49:41,959 --> 00:49:45,253
You have to choose between
that employee and me.

665
00:49:45,254 --> 00:49:47,755
Either take care
of the risky employee

666
00:49:47,756 --> 00:49:51,594
and finish the business with me securely,

667
00:49:52,177 --> 00:49:54,096
or take the risk and face ruin.

668
00:49:55,472 --> 00:49:58,225
Why should we trust you, Mr. Gi Su-jong?

669
00:49:59,268 --> 00:50:01,227
Well, trust isn't necessary.

670
00:50:01,228 --> 00:50:03,146
I mean,
when doing business in Korea,

671
00:50:03,147 --> 00:50:05,064
is there really anything to trust?

672
00:50:05,065 --> 00:50:06,609
Just feel free to use me.

673
00:50:07,192 --> 00:50:09,069
What's the value here?

674
00:50:09,653 --> 00:50:10,946
What are the risks?

675
00:50:11,405 --> 00:50:14,742
Just think of it from
a business perspective.

676
00:50:15,743 --> 00:50:16,951
At the very least,

677
00:50:16,952 --> 00:50:18,704
I work legally,

678
00:50:19,038 --> 00:50:20,372
so you'll like it.

679
00:50:25,586 --> 00:50:27,338
Hold on a moment.

680
00:50:28,088 --> 00:50:30,299
It's not a decision I can make.

681
00:50:31,425 --> 00:50:32,509
But right now,

682
00:50:34,303 --> 00:50:37,056
you know exactly
what I'm working on, right?

683
00:50:37,890 --> 00:50:39,391
Can you handle it?

684
00:50:39,850 --> 00:50:41,685
Yes, I can handle it.

685
00:50:42,478 --> 00:50:45,856
It's also a part I enjoy.

686
00:50:48,150 --> 00:50:49,109
So what do you say?

687
00:50:49,652 --> 00:50:50,402
Will you do it?

688
00:50:50,694 --> 00:50:51,654
Sure.

689
00:51:20,307 --> 00:51:21,557
Honey,

690
00:51:21,558 --> 00:51:22,810
can I ask you something?

691
00:51:24,436 --> 00:51:25,812
You

692
00:51:25,813 --> 00:51:28,482
promised me you'd never lie to me again.

693
00:51:29,191 --> 00:51:30,109
Remember?

694
00:51:33,320 --> 00:51:34,905
At the scene where Gyun died,

695
00:51:36,073 --> 00:51:39,326
did you really just
stand there doing nothing?

696
00:51:53,048 --> 00:51:53,674
Yes.

697
00:51:56,677 --> 00:51:57,553
I honestly

698
00:51:58,095 --> 00:51:58,929
don't know.

699
00:51:59,888 --> 00:52:01,390
I wasn't even there.

700
00:52:03,767 --> 00:52:04,935
Are you sure?

701
00:52:05,561 --> 00:52:06,311
Yes.

702
00:52:25,289 --> 00:52:25,998
Yi-gyeong,

703
00:52:27,750 --> 00:52:29,083
our family

704
00:52:29,084 --> 00:52:31,586
doesn't want you to be prosecuted.

705
00:52:31,587 --> 00:52:33,255
They told the police.

706
00:52:35,507 --> 00:52:36,717
Yes, thank you.

707
00:52:38,177 --> 00:52:39,720
Now you need to take care of yourself.

708
00:52:40,721 --> 00:52:43,974
They said they would
proceed investigating without arrest,

709
00:52:45,058 --> 00:52:47,853
so I should protect the baby
while on trial.

710
00:52:50,272 --> 00:52:52,608
If you need anything,
just let me know anytime.

711
00:52:56,320 --> 00:52:58,197
Still, you kept your word

712
00:52:58,822 --> 00:53:00,199
on the building and family.

713
00:53:02,034 --> 00:53:03,827
I've lost everything but this baby.

714
00:53:07,915 --> 00:53:09,374
Congratulations.

715
00:53:29,186 --> 00:53:32,606
I should have given it earlier.
I'm sorry. Just do what you want with it

716
00:53:38,862 --> 00:53:40,030
I don't need it anymore.

717
00:53:42,241 --> 00:53:43,867
I'm not one to hold grudges.

718
00:53:45,035 --> 00:53:45,911
But,

719
00:53:47,120 --> 00:53:48,831
things won't be the same as before.

720
00:53:52,793 --> 00:53:53,877
Yi-gyeong,

721
00:53:55,838 --> 00:53:58,799
apologies can't turn back time,

722
00:54:00,259 --> 00:54:01,176
but I'm sorry.

723
00:54:05,639 --> 00:54:06,557
Did you know

724
00:54:08,350 --> 00:54:09,935
how much I liked you?

725
00:54:13,689 --> 00:54:15,065
I just want to ask you one thing.

726
00:54:18,443 --> 00:54:20,571
I thought you liked me too.

727
00:54:22,406 --> 00:54:23,699
Was that all an act?

728
00:54:26,827 --> 00:54:28,537
No, Yi-gyeong.

729
00:54:29,454 --> 00:54:30,664
I can't act like that.

730
00:54:31,540 --> 00:54:33,333
I liked you too.

731
00:54:34,251 --> 00:54:35,627
And I still do.

732
00:54:38,088 --> 00:54:39,590
I brought this for you.

733
00:54:45,012 --> 00:54:46,638
It was with Hwal-sung.

734
00:55:22,507 --> 00:55:23,675
I'll be going now.

735
00:55:40,108 --> 00:55:42,361
ONE YEAR LATER

736
00:55:59,252 --> 00:55:59,962
Oh.

737
00:56:00,629 --> 00:56:01,254
Yes.

738
00:56:06,426 --> 00:56:07,219
Hello.

739
00:56:07,970 --> 00:56:08,929
Hello.

740
00:56:10,055 --> 00:56:12,556
Your iced latte without syrup is ready.

741
00:56:12,557 --> 00:56:13,558
Any move-in discounts?

742
00:56:13,892 --> 00:56:15,643
The boss said to just drink it.

743
00:56:15,644 --> 00:56:17,354
- Oh, thank you.
- Yes.

744
00:56:23,610 --> 00:56:24,361
Hello.

745
00:56:57,853 --> 00:57:02,566
CEO GI SU-JONG

746
00:57:10,490 --> 00:57:11,158
Mr. Gi,

747
00:57:11,825 --> 00:57:13,118
we're all set for filming.

748
00:57:13,744 --> 00:57:14,453
Yes.

749
00:57:16,580 --> 00:57:18,874
I don't have time to sweat.

750
00:57:20,167 --> 00:57:21,084
Where are we going?

751
00:57:21,209 --> 00:57:22,753
- Over this way.
- Yes.

752
00:57:26,465 --> 00:57:28,758
Having started from the bottom

753
00:57:28,759 --> 00:57:31,135
and becoming a property owner,
I am a very average

754
00:57:31,136 --> 00:57:33,388
family man in his forties
known as Gi Su-jong.

755
00:57:33,805 --> 00:57:34,764
Nice to meet you.

756
00:57:34,765 --> 00:57:35,890
Author Mr. Kim /
Gi Su-jong, CEO of Nouveau City

757
00:57:35,891 --> 00:57:40,394
You mentioned being
an ordinary family man in his forties.

758
00:57:40,395 --> 00:57:44,273
Let's start with how you first
got into real estate.

759
00:57:44,274 --> 00:57:45,399
Q. What made you buy a building
for the first time?

760
00:57:45,400 --> 00:57:46,692
It was a close friend...

761
00:57:46,693 --> 00:57:47,985
Right.

762
00:57:47,986 --> 00:57:49,154
He gave me a proposal.

763
00:57:49,905 --> 00:57:54,076
Every office worker
dreams of becoming a property owner.

764
00:57:54,576 --> 00:57:55,868
But in my case,

765
00:57:55,869 --> 00:57:57,245
I have a family.

766
00:57:57,454 --> 00:58:00,998
I thought about our future,
the future for my daughter,

767
00:58:00,999 --> 00:58:05,252
and how our family can have a better life,

768
00:58:05,253 --> 00:58:07,254
so we needed more income.

769
00:58:07,255 --> 00:58:11,051
That's when I thought, "What can I do?"

770
00:58:11,551 --> 00:58:13,385
And I decided,
"Let's invest in real estate."

771
00:58:13,386 --> 00:58:14,553
That's how it all started.

772
00:58:14,554 --> 00:58:15,387
I see.

773
00:58:15,388 --> 00:58:17,223
So, throughout your life,

774
00:58:17,224 --> 00:58:20,309
what was the best investment
that you made?

775
00:58:20,310 --> 00:58:21,018
Q. What was the best investment
in your life?

776
00:58:21,019 --> 00:58:23,229
My family.

777
00:58:23,230 --> 00:58:26,525
Yes, they were the best investment
that I've made.

778
00:58:27,025 --> 00:58:29,653
Um, my daughter...

779
00:58:29,986 --> 00:58:30,987
Um,

780
00:58:32,656 --> 00:58:33,697
she has hearing issues.

781
00:58:33,698 --> 00:58:34,574
Oh.

782
00:58:36,535 --> 00:58:41,038
She has significant hearing loss
and communication is tough,

783
00:58:41,039 --> 00:58:42,123
but she goes to Harvard.

784
00:58:42,124 --> 00:58:43,125
Yes.

785
00:58:43,708 --> 00:58:48,838
When I first wanted
to become a building owner,

786
00:58:48,839 --> 00:58:51,591
my daughter was my biggest support.

787
00:58:52,926 --> 00:58:53,885
And then

788
00:58:54,928 --> 00:58:58,305
that became my greatest strength.

789
00:58:58,306 --> 00:58:59,307
Right.

790
00:59:00,600 --> 00:59:02,685
There must have been someone
who helped a lot.

791
00:59:02,686 --> 00:59:03,603
Q. WHO HELPED THE MOST?
Um,

792
00:59:04,646 --> 00:59:07,022
I think I was really lucky.

793
00:59:07,023 --> 00:59:11,277
Yes, everything I've achieved so far

794
00:59:11,278 --> 00:59:13,530
is due to the help I received
from so many people.

795
00:59:14,030 --> 00:59:17,616
My wife especially

796
00:59:17,617 --> 00:59:20,077
has been my support

797
00:59:20,078 --> 00:59:21,997
and has shared so much with me.

798
00:59:22,247 --> 00:59:23,248
Yes, for that,

799
00:59:23,748 --> 00:59:25,542
I'm most grateful.

800
00:59:25,709 --> 00:59:27,126
"Writer Kim's World"

801
00:59:27,127 --> 00:59:29,253
is being watched all over the world.

802
00:59:29,254 --> 00:59:32,464
How about sending a video message
to your beloved wife?

803
00:59:32,465 --> 00:59:33,048
A surprise message.

804
00:59:33,049 --> 00:59:34,426
- To this camera?
- Yes.

805
00:59:35,427 --> 00:59:38,054
Uh, Honey...

806
00:59:41,892 --> 00:59:43,475
I'll call you later.

807
00:59:43,476 --> 00:59:45,186
Yes, I'll stop here.

808
00:59:45,187 --> 00:59:46,729
Oh, you're not doing it?

809
00:59:46,730 --> 00:59:49,023
No, I'll talk to her separately.

810
00:59:49,024 --> 00:59:50,232
- I understand.
- Yes.

811
00:59:50,233 --> 00:59:52,359
So, that was Gi Su-jong,
our guest for today.

812
00:59:52,360 --> 00:59:53,819
Thank you all

813
00:59:53,820 --> 00:59:55,654
for your precious time spent with us.

814
00:59:55,655 --> 00:59:57,406
That will be all for today.

815
00:59:57,407 --> 00:59:59,451
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

816
01:00:00,660 --> 01:00:02,536
- Good job, sir.
- Oh, thank you, Mr. Kim.

817
01:00:02,537 --> 01:00:03,538
- Thank you.
- Yes.

818
01:00:04,539 --> 01:00:05,749
- Thanks.
- Sure.

819
01:00:06,791 --> 01:00:08,626
Thank you for your time, sir.

820
01:00:08,627 --> 01:00:09,877
Oh, no problem.

821
01:00:09,878 --> 01:00:11,963
You made the request, so of course...

822
01:00:12,214 --> 01:00:13,965
Happy birthday, Mr. Gi.

823
01:00:14,591 --> 01:00:16,509
You shouldn't have.

824
01:00:17,260 --> 01:00:18,720
Have you spoke
with your daughter?

825
01:00:20,931 --> 01:00:22,556
Well, with the time right now,

826
01:00:22,557 --> 01:00:23,892
I'll have to call her separately.

827
01:00:24,935 --> 01:00:27,020
You should call your wife too.

828
01:00:27,395 --> 01:00:29,688
Thinking about the alimony,
before the building goes on sale again,

829
01:00:29,689 --> 01:00:31,024
it's better to start the divorce process.

830
01:00:31,733 --> 01:00:34,193
- It might be better to manage it...
- I understand what you mean.

831
01:00:34,194 --> 01:00:35,487
I'll take care of that myself.

832
01:00:36,363 --> 01:00:37,447
Sorry to bring that up on a good day.

833
01:00:38,114 --> 01:00:40,157
Enjoy your birthday.

834
01:00:40,158 --> 01:00:41,618
- I'll be leaving now.
- Yes.

835
01:00:46,957 --> 01:00:49,667
DAUGHTER

836
01:00:49,668 --> 01:00:50,627
VIDEO CALL

837
01:00:53,755 --> 01:00:55,048
THE CALL HAS ENDED

838
01:00:55,423 --> 01:00:56,049
What happened?

839
01:01:01,304 --> 01:01:02,138
SEON

840
01:01:08,270 --> 01:01:09,479
Why aren't they answering?

841
01:01:18,154 --> 01:01:21,157
GI SU-JONG

842
01:01:26,288 --> 01:01:29,082
Gosh, everywhere I go...

843
01:01:31,584 --> 01:01:33,210
- Mr. Gi?
- What?

844
01:01:33,211 --> 01:01:35,297
Did you finish everything?

845
01:01:36,006 --> 01:01:36,923
What's wrong?

846
01:01:37,215 --> 01:01:38,174
Guests have arrived.

847
01:01:38,758 --> 01:01:39,676
Who are the guests?

848
01:01:39,968 --> 01:01:42,554
I think it's Rep. Yong and another guest.

849
01:01:43,555 --> 01:01:44,764
- Let's go.
- Sure.

850
01:01:49,811 --> 01:01:50,602
EXPANSION CONFIRMATION! THE LAST WEEK!

851
01:01:50,603 --> 01:01:51,603
Thank you to all the guests
for visiting us

852
01:01:51,604 --> 01:01:53,898
WE'LL SEE YOU AGAIN AT PYEONG-BUK GWAN

853
01:01:55,483 --> 01:01:59,279
Oh, CEO Gi,
congratulations on your promotion!

854
01:02:00,071 --> 01:02:01,864
How about it? Want a drink first?

855
01:02:01,865 --> 01:02:03,365
Um,

856
01:02:03,366 --> 01:02:04,700
I'm currently working at the moment.

857
01:02:04,701 --> 01:02:06,202
- I'll come by next time.
- Sure.

858
01:02:07,037 --> 01:02:08,788
Enjoy your meal.

859
01:02:14,461 --> 01:02:15,420
Have you been doing well?

860
01:02:17,255 --> 01:02:19,632
I'm not sure how well I'm doing.

861
01:02:19,841 --> 01:02:20,800
How about you, Mr. Gi?

862
01:02:21,217 --> 01:02:23,385
Oh, I'm just the same.

863
01:02:23,386 --> 01:02:25,763
I'm just living well, you know.

864
01:02:25,764 --> 01:02:27,057
Hmm...

865
01:02:30,018 --> 01:02:30,934
Come by every week.

866
01:02:30,935 --> 01:02:33,521
Enjoy free large boiled pork.

867
01:02:34,564 --> 01:02:35,607
You seem close.

868
01:02:36,191 --> 01:02:37,025
Yes.

869
01:02:38,026 --> 01:02:39,569
There's an old saying.

870
01:02:40,320 --> 01:02:42,322
"A friend is near,
an acquaintance is closer."

871
01:02:43,531 --> 01:02:45,742
Oh, really?

872
01:02:46,534 --> 01:02:47,452
Enjoy.

873
01:02:57,087 --> 01:02:59,381
- Let's go talk. Come on.
- Let's go.

874
01:03:08,556 --> 01:03:09,766
Gosh, look at this.

875
01:03:11,726 --> 01:03:14,019
Such a lack of civic sense.

876
01:03:14,020 --> 01:03:15,145
Cigarette butts...

877
01:03:15,146 --> 01:03:17,482
I've had to clean this up so many times.

878
01:03:21,820 --> 01:03:25,615
I should just get rid of this ashtray.

879
01:03:28,576 --> 01:03:29,285
What is this?

880
01:03:32,372 --> 01:03:34,749
Gi Su-jong,
happy birthday!

881
01:03:47,595 --> 01:03:49,264
If I have these three...

882
01:03:52,350 --> 01:03:53,560
That's 15 million.

883
01:03:55,728 --> 01:03:58,606
COLLECTION NOTICE

884
01:03:59,691 --> 01:04:01,401
There's nothing left. Nothing at all.

885
01:04:03,153 --> 01:04:04,779
Just gotten bigger.

886
01:04:05,613 --> 01:04:06,739
Jeez.

887
01:04:09,993 --> 01:04:13,036
LUHA ELECTRICAL SERVICE: 862,000 WON

888
01:04:13,037 --> 01:04:13,746
TRANSFER COMPLETED

889
01:04:16,374 --> 01:04:18,208
DA-RAE'S LIVING EXPENSES: 4,000,000 WON

890
01:04:18,209 --> 01:04:21,295
Da-rae, save some money, will you?

891
01:04:21,296 --> 01:04:22,839
Seriously.

892
01:04:25,508 --> 01:04:27,093
JEON YI-GYEONG

893
01:04:33,892 --> 01:04:35,143
It's done.

894
01:04:37,687 --> 01:04:42,692
This month is your son's 100th day,
right? I added more

895
01:04:48,865 --> 01:04:51,701
Yes, happy birthday
to you too, Su-jong.

896
01:04:58,416 --> 01:05:00,001
Yi-gyeong, it's Su-jong.

897
01:05:01,002 --> 01:05:02,921
It's been a while, Su-jong.

898
01:05:05,131 --> 01:05:06,090
How have you been?

899
01:05:06,799 --> 01:05:07,926
How do you think it's going?

900
01:05:08,426 --> 01:05:10,803
Oh, you should be
doing well, right?

901
01:05:11,262 --> 01:05:12,722
I'm doing well.

902
01:05:13,681 --> 01:05:14,933
Better than ever.

903
01:05:16,976 --> 01:05:18,853
Oh, that's great to hear.

904
01:05:20,104 --> 01:05:22,565
Logan, want to hear
your uncle's voice?

905
01:05:24,108 --> 01:05:25,902
Hello? Is that you, Logan?

906
01:05:26,486 --> 01:05:28,904
Logan, can you talk?

907
01:05:28,905 --> 01:05:31,073
It's Uncle Su-jong.

908
01:05:31,074 --> 01:05:31,824
Logan.

909
01:05:33,535 --> 01:05:35,119
Uncle is a scary guy.

910
01:05:35,620 --> 01:05:36,955
You're smiling.

911
01:05:39,624 --> 01:05:41,376
How are Seon and Da-rae doing?

912
01:05:41,960 --> 01:05:43,877
Oh...

913
01:05:43,878 --> 01:05:46,838
Yes, they're doing well.

914
01:05:46,839 --> 01:05:49,384
We keep in touch regularly, once a month.

915
01:05:49,842 --> 01:05:51,093
But what's this?

916
01:05:51,094 --> 01:05:52,345
For you to give me a phone call.

917
01:05:56,558 --> 01:05:57,392
Well...

918
01:05:58,017 --> 01:05:59,519
Even so, I felt like

919
01:06:00,019 --> 01:06:02,522
I should reach out to you.

920
01:06:03,856 --> 01:06:05,441
I have something to ask you.

921
01:06:06,693 --> 01:06:07,443
Yes.

922
01:06:08,111 --> 01:06:10,280
Pyeong-buk Gwan
is moving, right?

923
01:06:11,489 --> 01:06:13,491
At the new hall,

924
01:06:14,826 --> 01:06:17,579
can I hang up a picture of my mom?

925
01:06:18,288 --> 01:06:20,039
You remember the photo
I sent earlier, right?

926
01:06:20,790 --> 01:06:22,500
Oh, of course.

927
01:06:23,376 --> 01:06:25,168
We have our banner

928
01:06:25,169 --> 01:06:26,461
all ready too.

929
01:06:26,462 --> 01:06:29,089
Once we move,
I'll print it in high quality

930
01:06:29,090 --> 01:06:31,426
and hang it up in a nice spot.

931
01:06:33,303 --> 01:06:34,137
Thank you.

932
01:06:35,722 --> 01:06:37,181
I hope people

933
01:06:37,932 --> 01:06:40,518
remember my mom in a good light.

934
01:06:42,270 --> 01:06:43,396
Oh, definitely.

935
01:06:43,646 --> 01:06:46,232
Ms. Jeon definitely deserves that.

936
01:06:47,900 --> 01:06:50,152
I still haven't forgiven

937
01:06:50,153 --> 01:06:51,486
that man named Gi Su-jong.

938
01:06:51,487 --> 01:06:52,614
Oh,

939
01:06:53,823 --> 01:06:55,992
I'll spend my whole life

940
01:06:56,743 --> 01:06:59,495
repaying the favor, Yi-gyeong.

941
01:07:00,121 --> 01:07:01,122
More than that,

942
01:07:02,415 --> 01:07:03,875
because of our mistake,

943
01:07:05,001 --> 01:07:07,629
Da-rae and Logan
can't get hurt.

944
01:07:08,921 --> 01:07:10,173
I want to live facing forward,

945
01:07:11,424 --> 01:07:12,925
not backward.

946
01:07:13,468 --> 01:07:14,302
Of course.

947
01:07:15,470 --> 01:07:17,262
I'll pray for you, Yi-gyeong.

948
01:07:17,263 --> 01:07:18,139
Yes.

949
01:07:28,691 --> 01:07:29,776
Come here.

950
01:07:38,910 --> 01:07:42,497
Seon, it's my birthday today.

951
01:07:44,499 --> 01:07:47,042
Even though we're far apart,

952
01:07:47,043 --> 01:07:49,212
I really believe we'll meet again.

953
01:07:50,421 --> 01:07:51,381
Oh, this is...

954
01:07:53,883 --> 01:07:54,926
The lines are bad.

955
01:07:56,761 --> 01:07:58,262
Hmm...

956
01:07:58,596 --> 01:08:03,475
How about we live our second act together?

957
01:08:03,476 --> 01:08:04,686
Shall we give it another shot?

958
01:08:06,437 --> 01:08:09,607
Jeez, is this going to work?
These lines...

959
01:08:11,192 --> 01:08:12,735
Let's give it a try.

960
01:08:21,619 --> 01:08:23,621
Is she still sleeping?

961
01:08:29,711 --> 01:08:31,921
I knew you would be here.

962
01:08:35,216 --> 01:08:36,050
Hey.

963
01:08:36,759 --> 01:08:38,260
Hey, buddy,

964
01:08:38,261 --> 01:08:40,555
why are you sitting here eating alone?

965
01:08:45,226 --> 01:08:46,144
Hwal-sung...

966
01:08:46,436 --> 01:08:48,312
You think I'd forget
my best friend's birthday?

967
01:08:49,021 --> 01:08:50,481
If you're thirsty for drinks,
you should've called me.

968
01:08:52,984 --> 01:08:56,279
Oh, that's right.
I got wind of an amazing opportunity.

969
01:08:56,738 --> 01:08:59,490
I was going to keep this to myself too.

970
01:09:00,450 --> 01:09:01,701
Want me to tell you?

971
01:09:02,410 --> 01:09:03,202
Yes.

972
01:09:03,911 --> 01:09:04,954
Wait a second.

973
01:09:06,748 --> 01:09:08,915
I just got my business cards made.
Take one.

974
01:09:08,916 --> 01:09:10,710
GI SU-JONG

975
01:09:44,660 --> 01:09:45,369
Dad?

976
01:09:45,828 --> 01:09:48,538
Hmm, what's seaweed in sign language?

977
01:09:48,539 --> 01:09:49,999
This one.

978
01:09:52,293 --> 01:09:54,462
I was boiling it like this.

979
01:09:54,921 --> 01:09:57,298
Did you have a birthday party?

980
01:09:57,632 --> 01:10:00,009
Uh, I had a drink

981
01:10:00,968 --> 01:10:02,011
with my friends.

982
01:10:02,220 --> 01:10:06,890
I'm sorry
I can't give you a gift on your birthday.

983
01:10:06,891 --> 01:10:08,266
Oh.

984
01:10:08,267 --> 01:10:11,646
Da-rae, you are the present to me.

985
01:10:12,772 --> 01:10:14,023
But what about Mom?

986
01:10:15,066 --> 01:10:18,068
She went out to
hang out with her friends.

987
01:10:18,069 --> 01:10:18,820
What?

988
01:10:20,404 --> 01:10:21,280
With who?

989
01:10:23,074 --> 01:10:25,952
There's this uncle
who's hairy and someone else...

990
01:10:26,744 --> 01:10:27,745
Hairy?

991
01:10:28,496 --> 01:10:29,288
Who could it be?

992
01:10:31,082 --> 01:10:32,208
Ta-da!

993
01:10:32,458 --> 01:10:32,958
Huh?

994
01:10:32,959 --> 01:10:35,002
Happy birthday, Gi Su-jong.

995
01:10:35,294 --> 01:10:37,672
We used your birthday
as an excuse to eat cake.

996
01:10:38,923 --> 01:10:40,091
Congratulations!

997
01:10:43,344 --> 01:10:44,345
Is that seaweed soup?

998
01:10:45,763 --> 01:10:48,099
You never made it once,
and now you do when you're alone?

999
01:10:48,808 --> 01:10:49,809
Well, I just

1000
01:10:50,726 --> 01:10:52,602
bought it at the store.

1001
01:10:52,603 --> 01:10:53,521
But how did you

1002
01:10:55,064 --> 01:10:57,483
remember my birthday?
Thanks for the birthday wishes.

1003
01:10:57,942 --> 01:10:59,401
Da-rae remembered.

1004
01:10:59,402 --> 01:11:00,695
That's my daughter.

1005
01:11:01,153 --> 01:11:03,530
You know Da-rae and I
are going to Seoul tomorrow. right?

1006
01:11:03,531 --> 01:11:06,324
Yes, I was thinking
of going to the airport.

1007
01:11:06,325 --> 01:11:07,827
No, it's fine.

1008
01:11:08,202 --> 01:11:09,954
We'll manage to get there. You're busy.

1009
01:11:10,413 --> 01:11:12,164
No, you have a lot of luggage.

1010
01:11:14,125 --> 01:11:14,876
Okay.

1011
01:11:17,753 --> 01:11:19,422
When we go to Seoul this time,

1012
01:11:20,089 --> 01:11:21,465
let's really get it done.

1013
01:11:21,841 --> 01:11:23,091
Oh my.

1014
01:11:23,092 --> 01:11:24,594
You're giving me a big birthday gift.

1015
01:11:27,221 --> 01:11:28,556
The timing is a bit off, right?

1016
01:11:29,223 --> 01:11:30,181
Sorry.

1017
01:11:30,182 --> 01:11:30,933
It's okay.

1018
01:11:31,601 --> 01:11:32,935
I've got all the papers ready.

1019
01:11:33,394 --> 01:11:36,355
If we break up now,
I think we could stay friends.

1020
01:11:36,898 --> 01:11:38,232
It's good for Da-rae too.

1021
01:11:39,358 --> 01:11:40,151
Yes.

1022
01:11:42,570 --> 01:11:44,030
Thank you, Seon.

1023
01:11:45,907 --> 01:11:46,782
Honey,

1024
01:11:47,825 --> 01:11:49,076
you've worked hard all this time.

1025
01:11:50,328 --> 01:11:52,455
I'm sorry and thank you.

1026
01:11:54,957 --> 01:11:56,375
Don't change too much.

1027
01:11:59,962 --> 01:12:02,840
Let's hang up since you're busy.

1028
01:12:03,090 --> 01:12:03,925
See you tomorrow.

1029
01:12:04,133 --> 01:12:05,592
Okay, got it.

1030
01:12:05,593 --> 01:12:06,385
Take care.

1031
01:12:20,358 --> 01:12:21,150
ATTORNEY ROBERT PARK

1032
01:12:25,237 --> 01:12:27,907
I need to talk urgently.
Call me back.

1033
01:12:36,999 --> 01:12:39,710
ATTORNEY ROBERT PARK

1034
01:12:50,805 --> 01:12:52,390
Why is he not answering?

1035
01:12:54,767 --> 01:12:55,559
What's this?

1036
01:12:56,227 --> 01:12:57,018
Notice of Gi Su-jong's ownership
of Nouveau City shares

1037
01:12:57,019 --> 01:12:57,852
and Seyoon Building, Han-maum Building,
Pyeong-buk Gwan auction procedures

1038
01:12:57,853 --> 01:12:58,979
A content certification
has been sent to your address

1039
01:12:58,980 --> 01:13:00,397
We ask for your cooperation,
and if you don't comply

1040
01:13:00,398 --> 01:13:01,524
please be aware that there
may be consequences

1041
01:13:04,443 --> 01:13:05,653
Is this phishing?

1042
01:13:16,414 --> 01:13:18,290
ATTORNEY YANG

1043
01:13:20,960 --> 01:13:22,336
OPEN THE LINK? CONFIRM

1044
01:13:26,090 --> 01:13:27,133
Gold Rush?

1045
01:13:31,303 --> 01:13:33,848
What's this?

1046
01:13:38,352 --> 01:13:40,187
Gold Rush Investment?

1047
01:13:41,022 --> 01:13:42,147
Nouveau City ownership, Seyoon Building,
Han-maum, Pyeong-buk Gwan related

1048
01:13:42,148 --> 01:13:46,317
A legal notice about the auction process
has been sent to your address

1049
01:13:46,318 --> 01:13:47,278
CONSEQUENCES

1050
01:13:53,034 --> 01:13:56,412
ATTORNEY ROBERT PARK

1051
01:14:06,797 --> 01:14:08,257
This guy isn't picking up the phone.

1052
01:14:09,425 --> 01:14:10,968
Are you Gi Su-jong?

1053
01:14:25,691 --> 01:14:29,111
Dad said
he'll be waiting in front.

1054
01:14:29,528 --> 01:14:31,030
I know, right?

1055
01:14:32,114 --> 01:14:34,867
Where did he go this time?

1056
01:14:49,006 --> 01:14:49,840
What are you doing here?

1057
01:14:50,925 --> 01:14:51,759
Me?

1058
01:14:52,635 --> 01:14:53,677
I started a new job.

1059
01:15:13,906 --> 01:15:14,907
Landlord, sir.

1060
01:15:18,953 --> 01:15:19,829
So, shall we

1061
01:15:20,996 --> 01:15:22,957
discuss some business?

1062
01:15:25,918 --> 01:15:26,752
Sure.

1063
01:15:27,920 --> 01:15:28,754
Anytime.

1064
01:15:31,674 --> 01:15:34,760
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

1065
01:15:43,686 --> 01:15:45,687
SPECIAL THANKS TO ACTOR JU JI-HOON

1066
01:15:45,688 --> 01:15:47,689
SPECIAL THANKS TO ACTOR PARK BYUNG-EUN

1067
01:15:47,690 --> 01:15:49,733
Special thanks to Kim Seung-wook
and Kim Do-yoon as author Mr. Kim

1068
01:16:41,619 --> 01:16:43,787
Thanks to everyone for watching
Mad Concrete Dreams

